  "name": "Example: Finding the Complex Conjugate of a Complex Number With Positive Imaginary Part",
  "problem": "What is the complex conjugate of $z=3+6\\textrm{i}?$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the complex conjugate, we flip the sign of the imaginary part.\n\nIn the given number $z=3+6\\textrm{i},$ the imaginary part is $6\\textrm{i}.$ Flipping the sign, we get $-6\\textrm{i}.$\n\nTherefore, the complex conjugate is given by $\\overline{z} = 3-6\\textrm{i}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
